A.practical=dict(graph='Plot open-circuit voltage vertically against the number of series-aiding identical cells horizontally.',unit='V per cell',meaning='The gradient estimates the open-circuit voltage contribution of one cell. The count axis is dimensionless; the slope can be described as volts per added cell.',method=['Check a high-resistance voltmeter’s zero, polarity and low-voltage range.','Measure one cell’s open-circuit voltage without a load.','Join a second identical cell in series-aiding orientation and measure across the outer terminals.','Repeat for the stated modest cell counts, checking polarity each time.','Repeat measurements and compare individual cells to assess variation.'],control='Use similar cells in similar condition, avoid short circuits, keep total voltage within safe classroom limits and do not connect a measuring ammeter across the cells.',table='Record number of series cells and open-circuit voltage / V, including repeated readings.',conclusion='An approximately straight near-origin voltage-count relation supports addition of similar source contributions; its gradient estimates one-cell e.m.f. under negligible load.')
